      "writtenOn": "2023-08-02T10:55:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My guess is, `available_profile.is_empty` doesn\u0027t equal to `!is_bonded`.\n\nLet\u0027s suppose we bonded to a device, but for some reason we fail to discover all the profiles. We potentially will now have a bonded device but empty available profiles.\n\nIf there is a reconnection:\n(a) initiated by the host: then we will try to re-discover the profiles again, so no problem I guess.\n(b) initiated by the peer: then we will not re-discover the profiles, and now it\u0027s up to the peer to actually connect the missing profiles.\n\nI suppose arriving at this state with empty available profiles does mean something bad happened so we potentially can work on a better strategy.",
      "parentUuid": "b9658bfa_f27a76d0",
      "revId": "72713d3c8d7596db39b47d03e2d4bc63189a2ada",
